	A \emph{conjunctive normal form (CNF)} formula is a propositional formula of the form $C_1 \wedge \dots \wedge C_m$ ($m \ge 1$), where each $C_i$ is a \emph{clause}, that is, a finite disjunction of \emph{literals} (variables or negated variables).
