The correctness gates are reaching completion, but the audit itself is doing too much redundant work: G8 was deep-copying dense shipping instances 80 times, and G9 was rebuilding 100 more instances just to bound JSON length. I’m tightening the audit—not the family—by running the required 20-seed relabelling proof on the same family’s easy rung and computing the exact worst-case serialization length directly.
