codex
Implemented a native Track-B Boolean RCSP generator based on Definitions 2.8–2.9 and Theorem 3.8 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.22914).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2511_22914.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/gen_2511_22914.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2511.22914/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes all nine gates:

- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact probability `1/12!`
- G6: five attacks, each 0/8; reference algorithm succeeds 8/8
- G8: 160 symmetry checks and 20/20 distinct unrelated keys
- G9(c): 60 characters, 12 atoms, 166 intended operations

STEP 4 remains infrastructure-blocked: every bare and G9 oracle request returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded.” Consequently, `submit.sh` correctly refuses to certify a hardness verdict. This is not a paper rejection, so no `REJECTED.md` was created. After replenishing the key, rerun:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2511_22914.py
```
